Z||000022||FieroHeather||06-13-2001||10:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>I was wondering how long it would take a woman to get in on this one. Your game Heather. 24, Beautiful woman and has balls to   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>From a mid thirties standpoint and personal experience yes girls when young are evil in the dating game. Unfortunately it is an evil only matched in volume by guys stupidity when young. Hey I been there I thought I was smart then too. Amazing what you learn as life drifts by...oops goes on I mean.<P>I think I lost the plot on my point there somewhere but oh well. Looks like the stupidity doesn't get better, do women become more evil Heather?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well AusFiero, I think there are exceptions to every case--and thinking that ALL girls are evil is potentially looking over the ones who may not be.  There are actually *some* of us who are intelligent, witty, accepting of themselves, and willing to work hard for what they have.  I guess if you asked grinthock, he'd have a biased answer, but overall, I believe that I possess those four characteristics mentioned above  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>As for evilness varying throughout the years, perhaps as teenagers, girls can be cruel to the boys they like/dont like.  It's all a part of the hormonal changes they are going through (just like guys).  <P>In the 20's, the trend is divided between those seeking to be married, and those "playing the game".  <P>The 30's are a time to settle down and get serious (career, relationships, family, house).  <P>40's is a different ballgame, where old lives are either left, or they are enhanced by the new experiences of starting over.<P>I think evilness sorta goes away, or just takes a different form in the dating world throughout the years.  I just know that I am very thankful to be the person that I am currently, and I am looking forward to what the future holds for me (single or married).||||reg||1
